# Per-service build-context filter, per ADR-0101 and ADR-0200. BuildKit reads this file
# next to the Dockerfile before any root .dockerignore. So each build states its own
# context rules, and no hidden repo-wide default exists. A Go service image compiles
# ONLY Go sources: go.mod, go.sum, libs/go, and services/*. The build context leaves out
# everything else. The frontend needs apps/ and libs/ts, so it has its own filter in
# apps/frontend/Dockerfile.dockerignore.
**/.git
**/.DS_Store
**/node_modules

# Non-Go workspaces and assets.
apps/
libs/ts/

# Repo plumbing that a service build does not need.
docs/
infra/
# The exception is the funnel definitions, which this image INCLUDES through the
# Dockerfile's COPY of infra/analytics/funnels.yaml. If an exclusion hides a file that
# the Dockerfile copies, review and lint do not catch it. The build fails with
# `failed to compute cache key: failed to calculate checksum`, which names neither
# the file nor this list. Include the needed path again, and do not narrow `infra/`.
# Then a new plumbing directory stays out by default.
!infra/analytics/
scripts/
tools/
.github/

# Root tooling and config that a service build does not need.
biome.jsonc
package.json
cog.toml
.golangci.yml
.rumdl.toml

# Markdown in any directory, including per-service READMEs.
**/*.md
